{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a metal-free, visible-light-mediated 3-component carbosulfonylation of alkynes using alkyl carboxylic acids and arylsulfinates. This photochemical approach converts sp-C to sp3-C to yield highly functionalized alkyl sulfones. The reaction utilizes 4CzIPN as an organic photocatalyst and is applied to the synthesis of sedum alkaloids, with a proposed mechanism involving two distinct photocatalytic cycles operating in tandem.",
